From fe69c509fad6add2ad08c1a0e9809fa7468e8598 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Serdar Kocdemir <kocdemir@google.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:03:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/42] Fix process-owned GL object tracking and cleanup leak

Recent changes moved GL object ownership tracking to EmulationGl using
RenderThreadInfoGl::m_puid, but RenderThreadInfoGl::m_puid was never
updated, as a result caused memory leaks when processes exit.

- Add RenderThreadInfo::setPuid() to synchronize m_puid across
  RenderThreadInfo, RenderThreadInfoGl, and RenderThreadInfoVk, and
  propagating m_puid in RenderThreadInfo::initGl().
- Restore the fallback to tinfo->m_contextSet in
  EmulationGl::createEmulatedEglContext() when puid == 0.
- Acquire mContextStructureLock and unbinding the helper context
  before erasing contexts in EmulationGl::cleanupProcGLObjects().
- Calls sweepColorBuffersLocked() during process GL object cleanup.

Bug: 559660099
Bug: 560140165
Test: bazel test //host:gfxstream_framebuffer_tests
Test: OpenglRender_unittests
Change-Id: Ib814de16ac98560028a44897fc2d24a42a19bd60
(cherry picked from commit a5b0def9cd0f858b3fc9e2fa88a11a6271f46b02)
(cherry picked from commit 3535eb53db97dab27daf7203317635fb0b97415f)

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#38
